//!
//! # A transport seam, and a pure core
//!
//! The socket lives behind [`{{Provider}}Transport`]; building the request and mapping the provider's
//! HTTP status to the right [`PortError`](pos_ports::PortError) are pure. That is what lets the shared
//! `{{Port}}` contract suite run in the fast pull-request gate against a stub, while the real TLS path
//! ([`Tls{{Provider}}Transport`]) is exercised in the gated integration lane and the soak — the split
//! ADR-0038 drew for the webhook sender and ADR-0058 for the couriers.
//!
//! # The exact provider wire is pinned in the gated lane
//!
//! The concrete endpoint paths, authentication, and vocabulary here are this adapter's own mapping;
//! the exact provider strings are confirmed against the live system in the gated integration lane.
//! What the fast gate proves is the port *semantics*, which do not change when a field is renamed.

